<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carlism</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1833–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carlism is a Spanish traditionalist and legitimist political movement that arose in 1833 in support of Infante Carlos María Isidro's claim to the throne against his niece Isabella II. Strong in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-navarre">Navarre</a>, the Basque Country and Catalonia, it defended <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a> and regional fueros under the motto 'God, Fatherland, Fueros, King'. It fought three <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlist-wars">Carlist Wars</a> and backed Franco in the Civil War.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carlism.jpg" alt="Carlism" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: .mw-parser-output .ubx-floatdefault[dir=&quot;ltr&quot;],.mw-parser-output .ubx-floatopposite[dir=&quot;rtl&quot;],.mw-parser-output .ubx... · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Spanish_Conservatism_Flags_Symbol.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
